<<~ ahu slot=`#/about`>>

! Relink Plugin — by Cameron Fischer (Flibbles)

A vendor declaration: this carrier names an outside artifact this tree carries, so a reader learns its
provenance and its terms without opening it.

''Author'': [[Cameron Fischer (Flibbles)|https://github.com/flibbles/tw5-relink]]
''License'': BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2019-2020 Cameron Fischer
''Upstream'': `flibbles/tw5-relink`
''Pinned commit'': `51266a1e853c616c5f0b401a9c881d518dddb9bc` (v2.6.2)
''TW5 plugin id'': `$:/plugins/flibbles/relink`

Relink replaces TiddlyWiki's own tags-and-list relinker. When a tiddler renames, it walks wikitext
links, transclusions, filters, macro and procedure parameters, and declared fields, and rewrites each
reference to the new title.

!! A packed offering

The packed bytes ride under `packages/lararium-tw5/offerings/relink/` (`offering.json`,
`relink-plugin.json`, `NOTICES.txt`), minted by `scripts/pack-relink-offering.ts` from the pinned
commit; a re-pack comes out byte-identical. The descriptor stays UNSIGNED: the operator signs it as
PUBLISHER through `lares nexus publish plugins source=packages/lararium-tw5/offerings/relink`. A
wiki loads it by naming the signed offering in its recipe's `plugin-offerings`; it never joins the boot
set, and `packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/` never carries it.

The optional `relink-titles` add-on stays out of the offering: it rewrites derived titles through
`wiki.deleteTiddler`, which escapes the rename door's dry-run capture.

!! Moving the pin

A new upstream version packs at a new commit, which mints a new offering. State the packed version in
`tw5-plugin-version` above in the same change, so the declaration never says one thing while the
offering carries another.

